# A ONE-BAR PHRASE SAVES WHAT IT PLAYS (0.17.48, the audit): the bar written into the line is the phrase's own bar, voice and accents (SEL held).
# Before, it was Capture's: the busiest of the last four bars of the voice on the page, accents on the beats, so a busy bar played before the
# phrase was saved in its place.
seed 0
wait 3000
turn SELECT 36 100
expect view 36
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect jamv 3
# a busy bar first, not recorded: six short keys
waitfor barstep 1 3000
key 0 down
wait 50
key 0 up
wait 150
key 2 down
wait 50
key 2 up
wait 150
key 4 down
wait 50
key 4 up
wait 150
key 5 down
wait 50
key 5 up
wait 150
key 7 down
wait 50
key 7 up
wait 150
key 9 down
wait 50
key 9 up
# the phrase: REC, two keys early in a bar (the first with SEL: an accent), REC ends it with that bar
tap REC
expect phrase 1
waitfor barstep 1 3000
press SEL
key 4 down
wait 50
key 4 up
release SEL
wait 250
key 7 down
wait 50
key 7 up
wait 100
tap REC
waitfor phrase 3 4000
wait 100
expect ph_n 16
expect bssteps 2
expect bsaccents 1
# let go: the line plays what was kept
tap REC
wait 100
expect phrase 0
expect bssteps 2
